<Article
  title="Privacy | ZeroBeatLabs"
  description="How ZeroBeatLabs handles your data, including static-site hosting, preview forms, and payments."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Short version: the static pages do not use our own analytics, cookies, or
    trackers. We receive information when you choose to contact us, request a
    preview, or buy a service, and we never sell it or add you to a mailing
    list. The preview forms and payment checkout use third-party services,
    described below.
  </p>

  <h2>What these sites collect</h2>
  <p>
    zerobeatlabs.org, the demo at demo.zerobeatlabs.org, and the website
    previews at web.zerobeatlabs.org are static websites. Their pages do not
    use accounts, our own analytics, cookies, or third-party tracking scripts.
    The interactive demo runs entirely in your browser; the data you edit there
    never leaves your device. This describes the sites themselves, subject to
    the hosting, preview-form, and payment-service disclosures below.
  </p>

  <h2>The website preview forms</h2>
  <p>
    On web.zerobeatlabs.org you can ask for a free website preview by submitting
    your business name, email address, and an optional message, and each preview
    page has a shorter form to leave just your email. We use those details only to
    reply and to build the preview you asked for, and we do not
    add you to any mailing list. Submissions are delivered through Web3Forms
    (operated by Web3Creative), a third-party form processor acting on our
    behalf. Web3Forms stores submissions encrypted at rest and may retain them
    for up to three years before automatic deletion. To block spam, it may send
    the submitter's IP address and email address to spam-filtering providers
    (CleanTalk and Akismet), and it runs on Amazon Web Services, Cloudflare, and
    Hetzner. Full details are in the
    <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" rel="noopener"
      >Web3Forms privacy policy</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The sites are hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub may log
    standard technical request information such as IP address and browser type
    for security and reliability. That data is handled under
    <a
      href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
      rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>
    When you choose to pay for a service, checkout is hosted by Stripe. Stripe
    collects payment and related checkout information under its own
    <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
    ZeroBeatLabs may receive the contact, billing, transaction, and limited
    payment details Stripe provides to us, such as payment status and the last
    four digits of a card where available. We use this information to provide
    and fulfill services, keep required accounting records, and handle refunds
    or disputes. We do not receive or store full card numbers.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    Booking and social links open third-party services, including Google
    Calendar. ZeroBeatLabs does not embed their content or send them information
    before you choose a link. Their privacy policies apply after you follow a
    link.
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email
    <a href="mailto:hello@zerobeatlabs.org">hello@zerobeatlabs.org</a>, we use
    your message and email address to respond and, if you become a customer, to
    provide and support the services you request. We do not add you to any
    mailing list, and we never sell your details.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
  <p>
    We never sell or rent your personal information. We may share it with the
    service providers described above, including GitHub for hosting, Web3Forms
    and its spam-filtering providers for preview forms, and Stripe for payments,
    as needed to operate the sites, respond to you, provide services, process
    payments, and meet legal or accounting obligations. We may also disclose
    information when required by law or to protect our rights, users, or
    services. We keep information only as long as reasonably necessary for
    those purposes, including recordkeeping, refund, dispute, and legal
    requirements.
  </p>

  <p class="note">Last updated 11 September 2026.</p>
</Article>
